    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31073" root="عول" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَائِلٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَالَ</span>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  One says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمْرٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَائِلٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَالٍ</span>, the latter being formed by transposition, meaning [<i>An affair,</i> or <i>event,</i>] <i>hard to
be borne, severe,</i> or <i>distressing,</i> and <i>great,</i> or <i>formidable.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَائِلٌ</span> applied to a measure of
capacity means <i>Exceeding others.</i> (IAar, TA in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عيل</span>.)

